{"answer":"For n=1, the sum is 1=1^2. Assume for some positive integer k that 1+3+\\cdots+(2k-1)=k^2. Then\n\n1+3+\\cdots+(2k-1)+(2(k+1)-1)=k^2+(2k+1)=(k+1)^2.\n\nThus the identity holds for k+1 whenever it holds for k; by induction, it holds for every positive integer n.","approaches":[{"description":"Mathematical induction: establish the base case and show that the identity at k implies the identity at k+1.","id":"induction-proof","outcome":"candidate","reason":"This supplies a self-contained proof for all positive integers."}],"change_log":[],"claims":[{"basis":"question_premise","basis_reference":"The question asks for the asserted identity for every positive integer n.","citations":[],"critical":false,"depends_on":[],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"domain-positive-integers","kind":"assumption","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"The required domain is all positive integers n.","step_ids":[],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Derived by the base case and inductive implication in the listed proof steps.","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":["domain-positive-integers"],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"odd-sum-identity","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"For every positive integer n, 1+3+5+...+(2n-1)=n^2.","step_ids":["base-case","inductive-step","induction-conclusion"],"tool_ids":[]}],"open_questions":[],"proof_steps":[{"citations":[],"depends_on":[],"id":"base-case","justification":"For n=1, the left side is 1 and 1=1^2.","statement":"The identity holds at n=1."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":[],"id":"inductive-step","justification":"Under the displayed equality, add the next odd number 2(k+1)-1=2k+1 to both sides: k^2+2k+1=(k+1)^2.","statement":"If the identity holds for a positive integer k, then it holds for k+1."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["base-case","inductive-step"],"id":"induction-conclusion","justification":"The base case and inductive implication establish the statement for every positive integer by mathematical induction.","statement":"The identity holds for every positive integer n."}],"question_status":"answered","tool_requests":[]}
